{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 42, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Toulouse and the ruler of the County of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Humberge of Toron and the nephew of King Baldwin III of Jerusalem.\n\n*Family and Early Life*\nRaymond III was born around 1140 and received a noble education. He was the heir to the County of Tripoli and was known for his military prowess. He was a skilled knight and participated in several battles during his early years.\n\n*Marriage and Children*\nIn 1152 Raymond III married Eschiva of Banyas and they had a daughter named Alice of Tripoli. However the marriage was short-lived as Eschiva died in 1168. Raymond III then married Raimonda of Antioch and they had a son named Bohemond IV of Antioch.\n\n*Conflict with the Crusader States*\nRaymond III had a complex relationship with the Crusader states. He was a vassal of the Kingdom of Jerusalem but often clashed with the king. In 1157 he participated in a battle against the Kingdom of Jerusalem and was defeated. He also had conflicts with the County of Jaffa and the Principality of Galilee.\n\nIn 1173 Raymond III was involved in a plot to overthrow King Amalric I of Jerusalem. However the plot was discovered and Raymond III was forced to flee to the County of Antioch. He eventually returned to Tripoli but his relationship with the king remained strained.\n\n*Later Life and Death*\nIn 1184 Raymond III participated in a campaign against the Ayyubid forces led by Saladin. The campaign was unsuccessful and Raymond III was forced to flee to the city of Tripoli. He died in 1187 during the Siege of Tripoli by Saladin's forces.\n\nOverall Raymond III was a complex figure who played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states. He was a skilled military leader but also had a reputation for being hot-headed and impulsive.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.015882885}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34376433}, {"token": " member", "logprob": -0.5870414}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.3748852e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00829915}, {"token": " House", "logprob": -0.27775657}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -5.483477e-05}, {"token": " T", "logprob": -1.9731891}, {"token": "oulouse", "logprob": -0.010144343}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.19851987}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.60799956}, {"token": " ruler", "logprob": -1.1838127}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0007836132}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.01429402}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -0.11035543}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.716599e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00026353702}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -0.00014780859}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.55001426}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.01670058}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -0.01647312}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.0010681406}, {"token": " until", "logprob": -0.1913093}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.09019204}, {"token": " death", "logprob": -0.0046049263}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.057685006}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0011993604}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -0.00034064212}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -0.00080183777}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.027841149}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.112268865}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.046947602}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.22220565}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.2033677}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.00058598036}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.15024479}, {"token": " II", "logprob": -0.0014892451}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.07499429}, {"